cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use or refer to Purna, please cite it as below."
type: software
title: "Purna: head-turn practice for left spatial neglect on Snap Spectacles, with a family and therapist web app"
abstract: >-
  Purna moves the cancellation exercise for left spatial neglect after stroke onto the person's own dining table
  through Snap Spectacles. Whole and chipped clay diyas measure egocentric and object-centred neglect; a bell from
  the left points to the side, never the answer; a replay and an attention map show where the search and the head went.
  Purna Family carries sessions to the family and the therapist, who can set the next session. A practice tool,
  not a medical device.
authors:
